# Assignment 1 – OWASP Top 10

## Description

The **OWASP (Open Worldwide Application Security Project) Top 10** is a standard awareness document that identifies the most critical security risks affecting web applications. It helps developers and security professionals understand common vulnerabilities and how to prevent them.

---

## OWASP Top 10 (2021)

| No. | Vulnerability | Description |
|-----|---------------|-------------|
| A01 | Broken Access Control | Users can access resources or perform actions beyond their permissions. |
| A02 | Cryptographic Failures | Weak or improper encryption exposes sensitive information. |
| A03 | Injection | Malicious input is interpreted as commands or queries (e.g., SQL Injection). |
| A04 | Insecure Design | Security weaknesses caused by poor application design. |
| A05 | Security Misconfiguration | Incorrect security settings expose systems to attacks. |
| A06 | Vulnerable and Outdated Components | Using software with known vulnerabilities. |
| A07 | Identification and Authentication Failures | Weak authentication mechanisms allow unauthorized access. |
| A08 | Software and Data Integrity Failures | Untrusted software updates or insecure CI/CD pipelines. |
| A09 | Security Logging and Monitoring Failures | Lack of proper logging and monitoring delays attack detection. |
| A10 | Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) | The server is tricked into making unauthorized requests to internal or external resources. |

